<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<templates xml:space="preserve">
    <t t-name="point_of_sale.PosConfigLnaChecklist">
        <div>
            <header>
                <h1>How to configure my printers</h1>
            </header>

            <section>
                <h2 class="mt-5 mb-3 pb-2 border-bottom">What is it?</h2>
                <p>
                    Local Network Access (LNA) is a Chrome feature that allows your browser to communicate
                    directly with your local network. It means you can make your browser communicate with
                    your devices without the need for importing certificates.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Be aware that it works only on chromium based browser: <strong>Google chrome, Microsoft Edge, Brave, Opera, Arc and others</strong>
                </p>
                <div class="alert alert-warning mt-4" role="alert">
                    <strong>We duly advise you to use Chrome or Brave browser.</strong><br/>
                    iOS devices (iPad, iPhones) are not compatible yet.
                </div>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="mt-5 mb-3 pb-2 border-bottom">How to configure my devices properly:</h2>

                <h3 class="mt-4 mb-2">Environment check</h3>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_chromium"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_chromium')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_chromium">My browser is chromium based (Chrome, Edge, Brave, etc.)</label>
                </div>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_browser_version"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_browser_version')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_browser_version">My browser is above version 142</label>
                </div>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_router"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_router')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_router">I have access to my router configuration (To fix device IP addresses)</label>
                </div>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_epson"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_epson')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_epson">I use an Epson printer (Check supported printers in Odoo documentation)</label>
                </div>
                <div class="form-check mb-2 ms-4">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_ethernet"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_ethernet')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_ethernet">My printer can be connected through ethernet cables (recommended)</label>
                </div>

                <h3 class="mt-4 mb-2">ePOS printers (Epson) configuration</h3>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_internet"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_internet')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_internet">Connect printer to internet (Ethernet cable recommended)</label>
                </div>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_ip"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_ip')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_ip">Printer's local IP address is printed</label>
                </div>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_printer_config"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_printer_config')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_printer_config">Access printer configuration panel by putting this URL in your search bar:</label>
                    <div class="mt-2">
                        <p class="mb-2"><code class="user-select-all text-break">http://[printer_ip]/cgi-bin/epos/service.cgi?devid=local_printer</code></p>
                        <p class="mb-2 text-muted">(Replace [printer_ip] with the printer IP address)</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_printer_firmware"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_printer_firmware')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_printer_firmware">Update the printer firmware</label>
                    <div class="mt-2">
                        <p class="mb-2 text-muted">The password is located on the back of the printer (remove covers).</p>
                        <img class="img-fluid d-block mt-2 mb-4 border rounded shadow-sm" src="/point_of_sale/static/img/lna_config/image.png" alt="Printer Password Location"/>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h3 class="mt-4 mb-2">Check printer reachability:</h3>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_printer_check"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_printer_check')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_printer_check">Access the below URL but replace [printer_ip] with your current Printer IP address</label>
                    <div class="mt-2">
                        <p class="mb-2"><code class="user-select-all text-break">http://[printer_ip]/cgi-bin/epos/service.cgi?devid=local_printer</code></p>
                        <p class="mb-2 text-muted">If this endpoint does not return a 404 error and displays a blank page, everything is ready.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h3 class="mt-4 mb-2">SSL/TLS &gt; Basic</h3>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_tls"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_tls')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_tls"><strong>Disable "Redirect HTTP to HTTPS"</strong></label>
                    <div class="mt-2">
                        <p class="mb-2 text-muted">Keep TLS settings enabled, otherwise the printer will not work with HTTPS.</p>
                        <img class="img-fluid d-block mt-2 mb-4 border rounded shadow-sm" src="/point_of_sale/static/img/lna_config/image_1.png" alt="SSL Settings"/>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h3 class="mt-4 mb-2">ePoS Printer Service</h3>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_epos_print"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_epos_print')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_epos_print">Check if <strong>ePOS-print</strong> is enabled</label>
                    <div class="mt-2">
                        <img class="img-fluid d-block mt-2 mb-4 border rounded shadow-sm" src="/point_of_sale/static/img/lna_config/image_2.png" alt="ePOS print enabled"/>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h3 class="mt-4 mb-2">Secure printing</h3>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_secure_print"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_secure_print')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_secure_print">If you have the secure printing setting, disable it</label>
                    <div class="mt-2">
                        <img class="img-fluid d-block mt-2 mb-4 border rounded shadow-sm" src="/point_of_sale/static/img/lna_config/image_3.png" alt="Secure printing enabled"/>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="alert alert-success mt-4">
                    <strong>Now your printer is properly configured to work with LNA</strong>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="mt-5 mb-3 pb-2 border-bottom">Enable LNA on your database</h2>
                <p>If your database is version <strong>19.1 or above</strong>, you can skip the system parameter section.</p>

                <h3 class="mt-4 mb-2">Before 19.1:</h3>
                <div class="ps-4">
                    <p>Add system parameter <code class="text-break">point_of_sale.use_lna</code> with a value of <code class="text-break">1</code>.</p>
                    <img class="img-fluid d-block mt-2 mb-4 border rounded shadow-sm" src="/point_of_sale/static/img/lna_config/image_4.png" alt="System Parameter Setup"/>
                </div>

                <h3 class="mt-4 mb-2">After 19.1:</h3>
                <div class="ps-4">
                    <p>Enable the “Use Local Network Access” checkbox directly on the printer configuration.</p>
                    <img class="img-fluid d-block mt-2 mb-4 border rounded shadow-sm" src="/point_of_sale/static/img/lna_config/image_5.png" alt="Printer Checkbox"/>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="mt-5 mb-3 pb-2 border-bottom">The printers are properly configured and the LNA is activated.</h2>

                <h3 class="mt-4 mb-2">Point of sale configuration:</h3>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_pos_link"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_pos_link')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_pos_link">Link your printers to your POS (ePOS)</label>
                </div>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_print"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_print')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_print">Open your POS and try to print a ticket</label>
                </div>
                <div class="form-check mb-2">
                    <input class="form-check-input cursor-pointer" type="checkbox" id="lna_prompt"
                        t-att-checked="this.checked('lna_prompt')" t-on-click="this.toggle"/>
                    <label class="form-check-label cursor-pointer" for="lna_prompt">The message will appear from the browser. <strong>Allow</strong> access</label>
                    <div class="mt-2">
                        <img class="img-fluid d-block mt-2 mb-4 border rounded shadow-sm" src="/point_of_sale/static/img/lna_config/image_6.png" alt="Browser LNA Prompt"/>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="ps-4">
                    <p>If the permission is denied, refreshing the PoS will show this notification:</p>
                    <img class="img-fluid d-block mt-2 mb-4 border rounded shadow-sm" src="/point_of_sale/static/img/lna_config/image_7.png" alt="POS LNA denied message"/>

                    <p>If the system parameter is set, but the browser doesn't support LNA, the PoS will show this notification:</p>
                    <img class="img-fluid d-block mt-2 mb-4 border rounded shadow-sm" src="/point_of_sale/static/img/lna_config/image_8.png" alt="LNA not supported message"/>

                    <p>If everything is correct, the Local Network Access status icon will turn green:</p>
                    <img class="img-fluid d-block mt-2 mb-4 border rounded shadow-sm" src="/point_of_sale/static/img/lna_config/image_9.png" alt="LNA Green Status"/>
                </div>
            </section>
        </div>
    </t>
</templates>
